First Author: Luo
Title: In silico perturbations provide multivariate interpretability in predicting post-lung transplant outcomes
Source number: 66

Very short summary: This retrospective US national-registry study analysed adult first-time lung transplant recipients from 1987 to 2022 and compared XGBoost with EHRFormer, a tabular BERT model, for predicting post-transplant outcomes. The best all-years model for 1-year mortality was EHRFormer, with a held-out test AUC of 0.64 (95% CI 0.61–0.66), accuracy of 60%, and F1-score of 0.64; both models showed limited discrimination despite identifying established risk factors.

